        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Quadratic reciprocity is the \"crown jewel\" of elementary number theory —\nGauss called it his \"theorema aureum\" (golden theorem) and gave at least\n8 proofs. It answers whether solving x² ≡ p (mod q) is related to solving\nx² ≡ q (mod p) — a non-obvious connection between two different primes."
    },
