        "root_concepts": "[quadratic, reciprocity]",
        "section": "number-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Quadratic Reciprocity",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DEFINITION:\n  (a/p) = 0     if p | a\n  (a/p) = 1     if a is QR mod p (a ≢ 0)\n  (a/p) = -1    if a is QNR mod p"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md#020",
      "path": [
        "04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:number-theory:04-quadratic-reciprocity, git-history:number-theory:04-quadratic-reciprocity]",
        "canonical_path": "number-theory/04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md",
        "concepts": "[quadratic, reciprocity]",
        "current_path": "number-theory/04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md",
        "id": "maxim:number-theory:quadratic-reciprocity",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "number-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[quadratic, reciprocity]",
        "section": "number-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Quadratic Reciprocity",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COMPUTATION — Euler's criterion:\n  (a/p) ≡ a^{(p-1)/2} (mod p)\n  This is +1 or -1 (or 0), so the congruence gives exact equality."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md#021",
      "path": [
        "04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:number-theory:04-quadratic-reciprocity, git-history:number-theory:04-quadratic-reciprocity]",
        "canonical_path": "number-theory/04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md",
        "concepts": "[quadratic, reciprocity]",
        "current_path": "number-theory/04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md",
        "id": "maxim:number-theory:quadratic-reciprocity",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "number-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[quadratic, reciprocity]",
        "section": "number-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Quadratic Reciprocity",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PROPERTIES:\n  Completely multiplicative: (ab/p) = (a/p)(b/p)\n  (a²/p) = 1 for all a with p∤a  (squares are always QRs)\n  (a/p) = (b/p) if a ≡ b (mod p)  (well-defined on Z/pZ)\n  Σ_{a=0}^{p-1} (a/p) = 0  (equal QRs and QNRs cancel)"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md#022",
      "path": [
        "04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:number-theory:04-quadratic-reciprocity, git-history:number-theory:04-quadratic-reciprocity]",
        "canonical_path": "number-theory/04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md",
        "concepts": "[quadratic, reciprocity]",
        "current_path": "number-theory/04-QUADRATIC-RECIPROCITY.md",
        "id": "maxim:number-theory:quadratic-reciprocity",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "number-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[quadratic, reciprocity]",
        "section": "number-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Quadratic Reciprocity",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXAMPLES:\n  Is 6 a QR mod 13?\n  (6/13) = (2/13)(3/13)\n  (2/13): 13 ≡ 5 (mod 8) → (-1)^{(169-1)/8} = (-1)^{21} = -1 → 2 is QNR mod 13\n  (3/13): by QR: (3/13)(13/3) = (-1)^{1·6} = 1, so (3/13) = (13/3) = (1/3) = 1\n  (6/13) = (-1)(1) = -1 → 6 is QNR mod 13. Verify: 6^6 ≡ ? (mod 13)\n  6² = 36 ≡ 10, 6³ ≡ 60 ≡ 8, 6^6 ≡ 64 ≡ 12 ≡ -1 (mod 13) ✓\n```"
    },
    {
